# Example: exposing Inimerse functions to Java (roadmap §3.2).
#
# Pipeline:
#   1. Define the interface once:      see examples/interface.def
#   2. Generate the JNI bridge:        python3 tools/bindgen.py interface.def --language java --out InimerseNative.java
#   3. Java exceptions <-> Inimerse errors: the generated wrapper throws
#      InimerseException when an Inimerse `error` crosses the boundary
#      (error conversion tested in tools/bindgen.test.py).
#
# func add(a, b) { return a + b }
# -> Java: InimerseNative.add(40, 2) == 42
say "see tools/bindgen.py --language java and tools/bindgen.test.py"
